[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   Step 141: SCLK signed-drift crossing channel (step_b105).
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   Step 096 tested the absolute calibration residuals -- the scatter
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   of the SCLK correction record -- and returned bounds at the ppm
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   level.  A different observable lives in the same record: the
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   signed fractional frequency offset dnu of the onboard oscillator
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   versus Earth time.  The onboard oscillator ticks in spacecraft
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   proper time; its measured rate against ground-defined ET through
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   the downlinked timestamps is a one-way clock comparison -- the
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   transport class the two-way cancellation theorem says can carry a
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   lapse signal.  This step tests the signed level for
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   crossing-aligned structure.
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   T1  Signed dnu level steps at the four boundary crossings
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   (V1 TS 2004.96, V1 HP 2012.65, V2 TS 2007.66, V2 HP 2018.90)
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   at 2/3/5-yr window widths, raw and smooth-ageing detrended
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   (quadratic in log mission-age).
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   T2  Changepoint extremeness: the same windowed-step statistic at
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   every admissible changepoint in each record -- the price of
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   asking "how often does a step this size occur anywhere".
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   T3  Joint statistic: 4/4 sign consistency against the measured
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   ~50 per cent negative base rate, and the Fisher combination
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   of the four negative-direction tail fractions.
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   T4  Artefact audit: calibration cadence around each crossing
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   (long gaps bias windowed means), and the NH1 interior control
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   (whose dnu is frozen at sub-0.1 ppm -- unusable for the
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   signed channel, registered as such).
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   T5  Degeneracy statement: ordinary oscillator ageing predicts
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   monotone deceleration, which the detrended test removes; what
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   remains is a crossing-aligned local feature, but the record
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   is kernel-segmented and two-craft, so the channel registers
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   as a candidate with priced degeneracy -- not a null and not
[2026-09-21 15:17:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 141]   a detection.
